Modifications
-------------

charnet/config/__init__.py
    Added resolve_charnet_paths() helper: resolves the WEIGHT, CHAR_DICT_FILE,
    and WORD_LEXICON_PATH config values against the charnet_src root directory
    so the package runs correctly from any working directory, without requiring
    users to launch scripts from a specific location.

charnet/modeling/utils.py
    Added rotate_rect_vectorized(): a fully-vectorised (numpy) equivalent of
    the original rotate_rect() function, operating on N detections at once
    instead of calling rotate_rect() inside a per-detection Python loop.

charnet/modeling/rotated_nms.py
    Added _aabb() and _aabb_overlap() helpers.
    Modified nms() and nms_with_char_cls() to apply a fast axis-aligned
    bounding-box (AABB) pre-filter before the expensive Shapely/pyclipper
    polygon-intersection computation, significantly reducing NMS runtime on
    pages with many candidate detections.

charnet/modeling/postprocessing.py
    Added BKTree and _BKNode: a BK-tree index built once over the lexicon for
    O(log n) edit-distance lookups instead of an O(n) linear scan per word.
    Vectorised parse_word_bboxes() and the character bbox computation using
    numpy operations, removing the per-detection Python loop.
    Added char_bboxes field to WordInstance (exposes per-character bounding
    boxes for downstream typographic analysis).
    Removed the filter_word_instances call from the forward pass (filtering
    is handled externally).
    Fixed numpy deprecation: np.bool → np.bool_.

charnet/modeling/model.py
    Added device parameter to CharNet.__init__() to support both CUDA and CPU
    (the original code was hardcoded to CUDA via .cuda()).
    Replaced the torchvision.transforms preprocessing pipeline with a custom
    pure-numpy / torch transform that avoids the unnecessary numpy→PIL→tensor
    round-trip of the original code.
    Added forward_gpu(): separates the GPU/CPU inference pass (with optional
    FP16 automatic mixed-precision on CUDA) from the CPU post-processing step,
    allowing batch pipelining in the surrounding code.
    Added postprocess(): convenience wrapper around OrientedTextPostProcessing
    for use after forward_gpu().
    Updated all .cuda() calls to .to(self.device) throughout.

tools/test_net.py
    Added CUDA/CPU auto-detection; passes device to CharNet and uses
    map_location=device when loading weight checkpoints, so inference runs
    on systems without a GPU.
    Added resolve_charnet_paths(cfg) call to handle relative config paths.


